nodecode-severian is a rewrite of Sahil-SS9's Sahil-SS9/Severian:

  https://github.com/Sahil-SS9/Severian
  commit bdb14b04ffa014148d4665f239688ca0856561da
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Sahil Saghir (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is plugins/hermes/severian of that commit, a thin
Hermes memory-provider shim over the repository's own engine, together with
the adapter it delegates to (src/severian/integrations/hermes.py) and the
HTTP API that adapter's engine serves (src/severian/api/). The cell keeps
the tool names and their jobs — severian_search, severian_ingest,
severian_get_observation and severian_search_shared — with
severian_get_memory reading one derived memory by id, which the API answers
and the provider reached in-process; the five-dimensional scope as the
security boundary, failing closed with no default scope; the shared read
over an explicit list of agent ids, merged and re-ranked exactly as
search_shared merges it; and the shape of a turn written to the store,
"user: ..." then "assistant: ...", as sync_turn writes it. The transport is
the engine's versioned HTTP API rather than a Python provider object, and
the agent calls the tools rather than having context prefetched for it.

What was left out, and why: correct and forget, because the HTTP API does
not route an observation revision or a memory correction, so they would
need either an in-process service or an endpoint the engine does not serve;
task progress, for the same reason; the in-process context assembler, which
has no HTTP route, so the model searches instead of being handed a context
block; and the Hermes provider lifecycle (prefetch, sync_turn, session
switching, delegation), which are Hermes's own interfaces — a finished turn
reaches the cell on the :frame point instead. LICENSE is the repository's
LICENSE, unchanged.
